# Universe content · galaxies
# researched: Wikipedia "Galaxy morphological classification" (Hubble sequence, de Vaucouleurs system); Arp, Atlas of Peculiar Galaxies; Galaxy Zoo (green peas)
# Real seeds for the galaxy generator: galaxy types, real examples, the parts
# galaxies are built from, the structures between galaxies, and the rules.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r05-universe.md

# ── Galaxy types (real) ──

# layout: how its stars are laid out: spiral (a disc with arms), barred-spiral (a bar with arms from its tips), elliptical
#   (a smooth ball of old stars: also cD, dwarf spheroidal, ultra-diffuse, radio and quasar hosts), lenticular (a disc with no
#   arms), irregular (clumpy, no order: also starbursts, blue compact dwarfs, green peas and merging pairs), ring.
# How each kind is grown (every one may be a range, a..b, each galaxy taking its own value from its seed):
#   layout: its shape (spiral, barred-spiral, elliptical, lenticular, irregular, ring). arms: how many spiral arms (none
#   given: 2 to 4 by chance). arm-spread: how loose its arms are (1 usual; ragged flocculent arms about 2.2).
#   star-forming-rate: how much it still makes stars (a spiral like ours 1), which sets its young clusters, glowing and dark
#   nebulae and remnants. structure-size: how much it holds against ours (giants about 3, dwarfs about 0.15).
#   globular-clusters: how many old clusters in its halo (ours about 160, a giant elliptical like M87 about 12,000).
#   bodies-on-arms: its young clusters and nebulae on its arms. bodies-spread: disc (a flat disc) or ball (a round swarm).
@galaxy spiral
name: Spiral galaxy
layout: spiral
real: yes
shape: flat disk with arms winding out from a bright central bulge
parts: bulge, disk, spiral-arms, halo, central-black-hole
stars: young blue stars in the arms, older stars in the bulge
gas: rich
star-forming: yes, in the arms
example: Andromeda Galaxy
star-forming-rate: 1
structure-size: 1
globular-clusters: 160
bodies-on-arms: yes
bodies-spread: disc

@galaxy barred-spiral
name: Barred spiral galaxy
layout: barred-spiral
real: yes
shape: spiral arms starting from the ends of a straight bar of stars through the center
parts: bulge, bar, disk, spiral-arms, halo, central-black-hole
gas: rich
star-forming: yes
example: the Milky Way
star-forming-rate: 1
structure-size: 1
globular-clusters: 160
bodies-on-arms: yes
bodies-spread: disc

@galaxy grand-design-spiral
name: Grand-design spiral
layout: spiral
real: yes
shape: two long, clear, well-defined arms
parts: bulge, disk, spiral-arms, halo
star-forming: yes
star-forming-rate: 1
structure-size: 1
globular-clusters: 160
bodies-on-arms: yes
bodies-spread: disc
arms: 2

@galaxy flocculent-spiral
name: Flocculent spiral
layout: spiral
real: yes
shape: many short, patchy arm pieces instead of a few long arms
parts: bulge, disk, arm-patches, halo
star-forming: yes
star-forming-rate: 1
structure-size: 1
globular-clusters: 160
bodies-on-arms: yes
bodies-spread: disc
arm-spread: 2.2

@galaxy elliptical
name: Elliptical galaxy
layout: elliptical
real: yes
shape: smooth ball or egg of stars, from round to stretched
parts: body, halo, central-black-hole
stars: mostly old and red
gas: poor
star-forming: little or none
example: Messier 87
star-forming-rate: 0.01
structure-size: 1
globular-clusters: 600
bodies-on-arms: no
bodies-spread: ball

@galaxy giant-elliptical
name: Giant elliptical galaxy
layout: elliptical
real: yes
shape: huge smooth ball of stars at the heart of a galaxy cluster
