@rule galaxy-hubble-stage
real: rule
says: galaxies run on a scale from smooth ellipticals, to lenticulars, to tight spirals, to loose spirals, to irregulars; any of them can be barred, ringed or peculiar

# ── Real examples ──

@example milky-way
name: The Milky Way
real: yes
type: barred-spiral
width-ly: 100000
stars: 1e11..4e11
center: Sagittarius A*, a black hole of about 4 million solar masses
note: our home galaxy, the Sun is in one of its arms

@example andromeda
name: Andromeda Galaxy
real: yes
type: spiral
note: the nearest big galaxy, heading toward the Milky Way

@example large-magellanic-cloud
name: Large Magellanic Cloud
real: yes
type: magellanic-spiral
note: a satellite galaxy of the Milky Way

@example messier-87
name: Messier 87
real: yes
type: giant-elliptical
note: home of the first black hole ever photographed

# ── Parts a galaxy is built from ──

@part bulge
name: Central bulge
real: yes
says: a thick bright crowd of mostly old stars at the center

@part bar
name: Bar
real: yes
says: a straight band of stars through the center

@part disk
name: Disk
real: yes
says: the thin flat plane holding most stars, gas and dust

@part spiral-arms
name: Spiral arms
real: yes
says: bright bands of young stars and gas winding out from the center

@part halo
name: Halo
real: yes
says: a faint round cloud of old stars and globular clusters around the whole galaxy

@part central-black-hole
name: Central black hole
real: yes
says: a supermassive black hole at the heart of most big galaxies

@part globular-clusters
name: Globular clusters
real: yes
says: tight balls of ancient stars orbiting in the halo

@part dust-lanes
name: Dust lanes
real: yes
says: dark streaks of dust along the arms

@part star-forming-regions
name: Star-forming regions
real: yes
says: glowing nebulas where new stars are born, mostly in the arms

@part tidal-tails
name: Tidal tails
real: yes
says: long streams of stars pulled out by a passing galaxy

# ── Structures between galaxies ──

@structure galaxy-pair
name: Galaxy pair
real: yes
says: two galaxies bound together by gravity

@structure galaxy-group
name: Galaxy group
real: yes
says: a few dozen galaxies bound together
example: the Local Group, home of the Milky Way and Andromeda

@structure galaxy-cluster
name: Galaxy cluster
real: yes
says: hundreds to thousands of galaxies bound together, filled with hot gas

@structure supercluster
name: Supercluster
real: yes
says: groups and clusters strung together over vast distances

@structure filament
name: Cosmic filament
real: yes
says: long threads of galaxies and gas, the strands of the cosmic web

@structure void
name: Cosmic void
real: yes
says: huge nearly empty spaces between the filaments

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule galaxy-seed
real: rule
says: every galaxy is generated live from the world seed (LAW 14); nothing is pre-built

@rule galaxy-size
real: rule
says: the player picks Small, Medium, Large or Massive; size sets how many star systems the galaxy holds, every one fully simulated all the time
systems-small: 100
systems-medium: 500
systems-large: 2000
systems-massive: 10000
decided: "Fewer, every one detailed" (docs/DESIGN.md, round 17)

@rule galaxy-type-pick
real: rule
says: the type decides which parts are used; spirals get arms, ellipticals don't, irregulars get patches

@rule galaxy-gas
real: rule
says: gas-rich galaxies keep forming new stars; gas-poor galaxies hold mostly old stars

@rule galaxy-arms
real: rule
says: young blue stars, nebulas and star-forming regions sit in the arms; old red stars sit in the bulge and halo

@rule galaxy-center
real: rule
says: big galaxies get a supermassive black hole at the center; some feed it and become active

@rule galaxy-neighbors
real: rule
says: a world can hold more than one galaxy; extra galaxies sit in pairs, groups or clusters along filaments, with voids between

@rule galaxy-collisions
real: rule
says: galaxies that pass close pull out tidal tails, may trigger a starburst, and can merge into one

@rule galaxy-satellites
real: rule
says: big galaxies are circled by dwarf and satellite galaxies

@rule galaxy-name
real: rule
says: only our own galaxy is the Milky Way and only our own star is the Sun; generated ones get generated names
